Package: NCVROC
Type: Package
Title: Nested Cross-Validation for Combinatorial ROC-Based Selection of Item-Set Scores
Version: 0.15.0
Authors@R:
    person(
        given = "Sohei",
        family = "Ide",
        email = "sohei@ni.tama.ac.jp",
        role = c("aut", "cre", "cph")
    )
Description: Develops short item-based screening scales through combinatorial
    item-set selection, receiver operating characteristic (ROC) curve
    evaluation, ordinary and nested cross-validation, and selection optimism
    assessment. For questionnaire data, identifies which subset of items best
    predicts a binary outcome using unweighted sum scores. Supports fixed-model
    k-fold and leave-one-out cross-validation, cross-size combinatorial search,
    nested cross-validation for selection procedure generalization assessment,
    and comparison of non-nested and nested model selection performance.
    Methods for ROC analysis are described by Fawcett (2006)
    <doi:10.1016/j.patrec.2005.10.010>, and nested cross-validation by
    Varma and Simon (2006) <doi:10.1186/1471-2105-7-91>.
